Original commit body from c9caeab:

This commit tests the fix we just implemented for preserving commit
message bodies during squash merge. The fix had two components:

1. Added .forgejo/default_merge_message/SQUASH_TEMPLATE.md which tells
   Forgejo to use ${PullRequestTitle} and ${PullRequestDescription}
   placeholders when constructing squash merge commit messages.

2. Fixed scripts/auto-pr to preserve newlines in commit descriptions:
   - Removed the tr/sed pipeline that collapsed the body to one line
   - Removed explicit newline stripping in do_pr() and flush_queue()
   - Added proper JSON escaping for newlines in the vPR queue

If this commit body appears in the final squash merge commit on dev,
then the fix is working correctly. The previous behavior would have
collapsed this entire message into a single ~118 character line
containing only the subject and Co-authored-by trailers.
